msgstr ""

msgid "From 3 to 12."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sales mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "For the whole shop. A product category or a single product can choose its own mode; when a product is in several categories, the strictest one applies. Hidden prices are left out of the page, the shop data and the structured data, and the products cannot be added to the cart."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sale: prices and the cart for everyone"
msgstr ""

msgid "Prices for logged-in customers only"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quote: no prices, customers ask for an offer"
msgstr ""

msgid "Catalog: products only, no prices"
msgstr ""

msgid "WhatsApp number"
msgstr ""

msgid "With the country code, e.g. +90 532 000 00 00. The Product enquiry block links to a chat with this number. Its phone link uses the phone number of the brand."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contact page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Address of the page the Product enquiry block links to, e.g. the contact page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Show the mini cart in the header"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adds the cart button after the menu in the theme headers. It shows the number of items and opens the cart in a side panel."
msgstr ""

msgid "Load classic WooCommerce files only where they are used"
msgstr ""

msgid "The classic WooCommerce styles and jQuery scripts load on account pages, on pages with a WooCommerce shortcode and with classic templates. The theme shop templates are made of blocks, which bring their own files."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn off cart fragments"
msgstr ""

msgid "An old script that asks the server for the cart on every page view. The mini cart block does not need it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wishlist"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adds a heart button to product cards and product pages. Visitors keep their list in the browser; a logged-in customer's list is kept in their account."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wishlist page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Address of the page that shows the list with the Wishlist block. With an address, the theme headers link to it and show the number of saved products."
msgstr ""

msgid "Compare"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adds a compare button to product cards and product pages. Up to four products, kept in the visitor's browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "Compare page"
msgstr ""

msgid "Address of the page that shows the products side by side with the Compare block. With an address, the theme headers link to it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Theme style for product options"
msgstr ""

msgid "Gives the colour swatches and option buttons of variable products the theme's look: larger touch targets, a clear ring on the chosen and the focused option, unavailable options crossed out, and the chosen colour's name under the swatches. For colour swatches, turn on \"Color swatches for attributes\" under WooCommerce → Settings → Advanced → Features and give the attribute the \"Color / image\" type."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sticky add-to-cart bar"
msgstr ""

msgid "When the add-to-cart button scrolls out of view on a product page, a bar with the product's image, name, price and button appears at the bottom of the screen. For a product with options it first takes the visitor to the options."
msgstr ""

msgid "Back-in-stock alerts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sold-out products and options show a form where visitors leave their email address; when the product is back in stock, each address gets one email. Visitors who are not logged in first confirm their address with a link we email them. The addresses are listed under WooCommerce → Stock alerts, and both emails can be edited under WooCommerce → Settings → Emails."
msgstr ""

msgid "Size guide"
msgstr ""

msgid "A \"Size guide\" button above the add-to-cart button opens the guide in a window. A guide is a synced pattern made under Appearance → Editor → Patterns; choose it on a product category (its subcategories and products follow) or on a product, under Product data → General. Products without a guide show nothing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Frequently bought together"
msgstr ""

msgid "Under the add-to-cart button, the product and up to three of its cross-sells (Product data → Linked products) with checkboxes, a total and one button that adds the chosen ones to the cart. Cross-sells with options get a link to their page. Each product keeps its own price."
msgstr ""

msgid "Show the estimated delivery date"
msgstr ""

msgid "Product pages show a date range under the add-to-cart button, and before the cut-off time on a working day also that an order ships today. It is worked out in the visitor's browser from the settings below, so it stays right on cached pages. Not shown for virtual, sold-out or hidden products."
msgstr ""

msgid "Order cut-off time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Orders placed on a working day before this time count as placed that day; later ones count from the next working day. In the site's time zone (Settings → General). Leave empty for no cut-off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Days to prepare an order"
msgstr ""

msgid "Working days from the order until it is handed to the carrier. 0: it ships the same day."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shortest delivery time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Working days the carrier needs at best. A shipping class can set its own delivery time under WooCommerce → Settings → Shipping → Classes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Longest delivery time"
msgstr ""

msgid "Working days the carrier needs at most."
msgstr ""

